{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgV93SikafjTkQdRExgGM", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01XetGHyT2ZwbzkDYfdDcjbZ", "name": "Edit", "input": {"replace_all": false, "file_path": "/tmp/skilldiff-06r5ho42/ws/README.md", "old_string": "## Development\n", "new_string": "## Payments module\n\n`shop/payments.py` calculates order totals, tax, and refunds. All amounts\nare plain numbers in the shop's currency; the module does no rounding except\nin `order_total`.\n\n### Constants\n\n- `TAX_RATE` (`0.0825`): the sales tax rate applied to every order total.\n\n### Functions\n\n- `line_total(price, quantity)`: returns `price * quantity` for one line item.\n- `order_total(lines)`: takes a list of `(price, quantity)` tuples, sums the\n  line totals, applies `TAX_RATE`, and returns the result rounded to 2 places.\n- `refund(order_total_amount, amount)`: returns the remaining balance,\n  `order_total_amount - amount`. It does not check that `amount` is positive\n  or no larger than the order total.\n\n### Example\n\n```python\nfrom shop.payments import order_total, refund\n\ntotal = order_total([(10.00, 2), (5.50, 1)])  # (25.50) * 1.0825 = 27.6038 -> 27.6\nremaining = refund(total, 7.60)               # 27.6 - 7.6 = 20.0\n```\n\n## Development\n"}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 611, "cache_read_input_tokens": 39536, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 611}, "output_tokens": 5, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-28T18:52:02.558Z", "request_id": "req_011CgV93SBmApPcqpsTq4e8Q", "wire_tool_inputs": {"toolu_01XetGHyT2ZwbzkDYfdDcjbZ": {"file_path": "/tmp/skilldiff-06r5ho42/ws/README.md", "old_string": "## Development\n", "new_string": "## Payments module\n\n`shop/payments.py` calculates order totals, tax, and refunds. All amounts\nare plain numbers in the shop's currency; the module does no rounding except\nin `order_total`.\n\n### Constants\n\n- `TAX_RATE` (`0.0825`): the sales tax rate applied to every order total.\n\n### Functions\n\n- `line_total(price, quantity)`: returns `price * quantity` for one line item.\n- `order_total(lines)`: takes a list of `(price, quantity)` tuples, sums the\n  line totals, applies `TAX_RATE`, and returns the result rounded to 2 places.\n- `refund(order_total_amount, amount)`: returns the remaining balance,\n  `order_total_amount - amount`. It does not check that `amount` is positive\n  or no larger than the order total.\n\n### Example\n\n```python\nfrom shop.payments import order_total, refund\n\ntotal = order_total([(10.00, 2), (5.50, 1)])  # (25.50) * 1.0825 = 27.6038 -> 27.6\nremaining = refund(total, 7.60)               # 27.6 - 7.6 = 20.0\n```\n\n## Development\n"}}}
